      guideFront: "Choose a strategy when...",
      guideBack: "One way it could sound",
      description: "Supporting friends, neighbors, or colleagues going through personal tragedy or severe life strain requires quiet presence rather than shallow optimism or unsolicited advice.\n\n• Validate deep personal strain without offering cliché solutions\n• Share reciprocal vulnerability to honor their emotional weight\n• Offer specific, low-friction support goals\n\nMindset: Grief requires shared presence, not premature comfort.",
